    [
     3,
     "<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">El martes, 29 de octubre de 2024 a las 15:39:45 UTC, Eric Rexstad escribió:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nHello Elena</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nWelcome to the list.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nAppreciate you providing a bit of your data so I could diagnose your problem. You don&#39;t indicate whether the survey you conducted was lines or points; I&#39;ll presume lines, but the answer to that question does not influence the problem you are having.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nI think the reason R might be offering a complaint is because of the use of &quot;,&quot; as the decimal separator in your Area, Effort and distance fields. Adding the argument &quot;dec&quot; to the &quot;read.table&quot; function resolves this issue. I make a file named &quot;elena.txt&quot; from\r\n the lines of data you sent and wrote the following few lines of code, running the code did not generate the warning about a missing &quot;distbegin&quot; column.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nmydata &lt;- read.table(&quot;E:/troubleshoot/Elena/elena.txt&quot;, header=TRUE, <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,0)\">\r\ndec=&quot;,&quot;</span>)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nlibrary(Distance)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\ntest &lt;- ds(data = mydata, key=&quot;hn&quot;)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nsummary(test)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos Mono,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,monospace;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nplot(test)</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nHopefully that solves your problem and you can carry on with your analyses.  Let us know if anything else arises.</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" style=\"font-size:11pt\" color=\"#000000\"><b>From:</b> <a rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; on behalf of elena jimenez &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">elenajime...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> 29 October 2024 12:11<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> distance-sampling &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [distance-sampling] Warning: Unknown or uninitialised column: `distbegin`.</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi distancesamplers :)\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div> I am currently working with urban bird populations in city centers and encountering the warning\r\n<i>&#39;Unknown or uninitialized column: distbegin.</i>&#39; when processing my dataset with the &#39;ds&#39; function, which I am unable to fully understand or resolve. My dataset appears as follows:</div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Region.Label<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Area<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\r\n</span>Sample.Label<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Effort<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\r\n</span>object<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>distance<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\r\n</span>size<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>behaviour<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\r\n</span>month<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>Study.Area<br>\r\nTuristico<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>1,73395<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\r\n</span>3<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>1,2<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>\r\n1<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>0<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>3<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\r\n</span>1<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>May<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>\r\nFunchal<br>\r\nTuristico<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>1,73395<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\r\n</span>8<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>1,2<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>\r\n2<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>0,5<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>1<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\r\n</span>0<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>May<span style=\"white-space:pre\"> </span>\r\nFunchal<br>\r\nTuristico<span style=\"white-space:pre\